                    insight_cleared:        `Viability gate cleared: you held access and viability together — a tiered, promoter-delivered offer, a credible certification, a cross-subsidy that widened reach, and a declining-subsidy path to break-even. The investor releases the tranche and the poorest keep their care.`,
                    insight_pricedout:      `You priced out the poor: a fee increase lifted margin but collapsed the access index for the poorest quintile, with too little cross-subsidy to catch the dropouts. You optimised viability and failed the half of the gate that is the mission.`,
                    insight_subsidytrap:    `Subsidy trap: you reached more patients by underpricing, but with no declining-subsidy path the Q4.0M tranche runs down against a deficit. Charity that runs out of money closes clinics in year three — the gate exists to prevent exactly this.`,
                    insight_short:          `You didn't fully reconcile the three gate conditions. Access, viability and the ESG rating still pull in different directions — enough for the board to see the plan doesn't quite hold together.`,
                    insight_blended:        `Your ESG / social rating cleared the bar — that unlocks up to Q6M of blended co-financing on top of the tranche, your cheapest growth capital. Treating the rating as a design driver paid for itself.`,
                    insight_noblended:      `Your ESG rating stayed below the bar, so the up-to-Q6M blended co-financing never unlocked. You left your cheapest source of growth capital on the table by treating the rating as paperwork.`,
                    insight_nocert:         `Skipping certification cost you more than the Q250K you saved: referral NGOs and the rating analyst had no external quality signal to trust, and gate risk stayed high. In a weak-institution market, the cost of not being trusted is the patients you never reach.`,
                    insight_noavail:        `Your offer never solved availability: with almost nothing delivered through community promoters, the half of your target who live hours from a clinic stayed unreached. Affordability without availability still equals zero patients reached.`,
                    insight_deficit:        `Your viability went negative — the plan burns cash faster than the tranche can cover. Either an over-broad offer or an underpriced cut with too little cross-subsidy means break-even within 18 months is not credible.`,
                    insight_trusted:        `Access is high, the ESG rating is strong and gate risk is low — the social claim is now substantiated and verifiable rather than asserted. That is what releases the tranche and the blended co-financing on top of it.`,
